# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this, every `docker build` uploads the whole working tree to the daemon
# before it discards most of it. On this machine that is ~590 MB, of which ~589 MB
# is `.venv` and `.mypy_cache`: the build context arrives, `pip wheel` runs, and
# nothing from either directory is ever copied into the image.
#
# It also makes the image's contents depend on what happens to be in the working
# directory. `.env` holding a real key, or `data/published/` holding pull requests
# from a previous `python -m backend.scripts.run_remediation`, would both be copied
# in. An image whose contents vary with the developer's shell is not reproducible.

# --- Virtual environments ------------------------------------------------
# A Windows build here and a Linux one in the image. Beyond the dead weight,
# `/app/.venv` would be found before the installed site-packages, so copying it in
# is a live hazard rather than only a waste of bandwidth.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Version control and CI ----------------------------------------------
# The build copies named directories, not the repository. `.git` is also large and
# never needed in a layer.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- Local environment ----------------------------------------------------
# `.env` is gitignored and its API key is empty on a fresh checkout, but "it
# happens to be empty right now" is not a property to bake into an image: this is
# the one entry that could leak a real credential into a published layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Caches ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.cover

# --- Generated data inside the copied `data/` tree ------------------------
# `data/` as a whole is NOT excluded: the Dockerfile copies it, and the CVE feed,
# the scanner fixtures, the deliberately-vulnerable sample app, the telemetry
# contract and the evidence corpus are all runtime or test inputs. These two
# subdirectories are generated, and the second one is the expensive one --
# `backend/evidence/tier3.py` shallow-clones upstream repositories per advisory,
# so a run leaves a few hundred megabytes of someone else's source in the working
# tree. See the matching note in .gitignore.
data/published/
data/evidence/.cache/
data/telemetry/*.jsonl
!data/telemetry/events.jsonl

# --- Not copied into the image -------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile copies named directories, so everything below is dead weight.
# `docs/` is excluded by name rather than by `*.md`, because `README.md` is
# explicitly copied and `.dockerignore` cannot re-include a file whose parent is
# excluded.
docs/
Makefile
LICENSE
docker/

# Generated gRPC stubs under `backend/grpc_service/generated/` are committed on
# purpose (CLAUDE.md: nothing warns you if they go stale), so they are
# deliberately NOT excluded.

# --- Editor and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
